{"id":"s1.5.2","slug":"switching-numbers-and-negating-on-subtraction","title":"Switching Numbers and Negating on Subtraction","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">When a subtraction problem results in a negative answer (e.g., subtracting a larger number from a smaller one), it's often easier to switch the order of the numbers, perform the subtraction, and then negate the result.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">This uses the principle $a - b = -(b - a)$.</p><p>For example, to calculate $4\\frac{5}{6} - 10\\frac{11}{12}$, you can instead calculate $-(10\\frac{11}{12} - 4\\frac{5}{6})$. This simplifies the process by avoiding borrowing across the whole number in a negative context.</p><p>$ -(10\\frac{11}{12} - 4\\frac{10}{12}) = -(6\\frac{1}{12}) $.</p>","summary":"When a subtraction problem results in a negative answer (e.g., subtracting a larger number from a smaller one), it's often easier to switch the order","generation_guideline":"Generate a subtraction problem with mixed numbers where the second number is larger than the first.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $2\\frac{2}{3} - 3\\frac{5}{6}$. (mixed number)","answer":"-1 1/6","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $4\\frac{2}{3} - 6\\frac{3}{5}$. (mixed number)","answer":"-1 14/15","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $1\\frac{5}{9} - 3\\frac{5}{9}$.","answer":"-2","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $2\\frac{3}{4} - 4\\frac{3}{5}$. (mixed number)","answer":"-1 17/20","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $1\\frac{3}{7} - 3$. (mixed number)","answer":"-1 4/7","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $2\\frac{3}{8} - 3\\frac{1}{4}$.","answer":"-7/8","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $2\\frac{3}{4} - 6\\frac{